        "id": 1550939
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-27T18:11:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t mean \"shared\", because Soong doesn\u0027t know what it is (it doesn\u0027t have the information in /system/etc/permissions/platform.xml).\n\nWhat I mean is, all dependencies that have OptionalImplicitSdkLibrary (possibly transitive). That\u0027s how it is computed in Soong.\n\nAs far as I understand, all such libraries have to be \"shared\". We are not checking this in Soong, and we didn\u0027t check before my work on class loader contexts, while manifest_fixer existed before that. Should we generate checks similar to verify_uses_libraries.sh that will parse /system/etc/permissions/platform.xml and fail if we try to add something in the manifest (or CLC) that is not in that file? Will that work for vendor libraries?\n\nFor now I documented that we do not check \"shared\".",
      "parentUuid": "c055168c_c233fb46",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 134,
        "startChar": 79,
        "endLine": 134,
        "endChar": 90
      },
      "revId": "48891a95c5de7b178885419bb05b4069c1051444",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
